<Project>

  <!--
    ============================================================================
    Keep .aar files out of lib/<tfm>/
    ============================================================================
    Applies to every project in the repository, because the problem shows up at two different
    levels and the fix is identical:

      Red5Pro.Streaming.Net.Android   binds red5-android-sdk.aar and webrtc-android.aar, and .NET
                                      for Android packs every bound .aar into lib/<tfm>/ by
                                      default. Pack="false" on the AndroidLibrary item is silently
                                      ignored.

      Red5Pro.Streaming.Net, .Maui    reference that package, and the transitively restored .aar is
                                      packed into *their* lib/<tfm>/ too - so libwebrtc appeared
                                      three more times at 45 MB each, taking the dependency-only
                                      cross-platform package to 83 MB.

    Two reasons to stop it, one mechanism:

      red5-android-sdk.aar   must not ship at all. The Red5 EULA forbids redistributing it
                             (3.6, 3.7), and the default behaviour would have published it inside
                             a public NuGet package.
      webrtc-android.aar     may ship, and does - but once, from native/ in the Android package,
                             rather than nine times across four packages.

    The filter hooks _IncludeAarInNuGetPackage, which is the .NET for Android target that adds
    them; the items arrive as TfmSpecificPackageFileWithRecursiveDir, not TfmSpecificPackageFile.
    Both of those facts were established by dumping the item groups at pack time - guessing the
    hook produced a package that looked right and was not.

    Red5Pro.Streaming.Net.PackageTests asserts the outcome on the packed .nupkg, because this is
    exactly the kind of thing that silently regresses when the Android SDK changes its packing.
  -->
  <Target Name="Red5FilterPackagedAars" AfterTargets="_IncludeAarInNuGetPackage">
    <ItemGroup>
      <TfmSpecificPackageFileWithRecursiveDir
          Remove="@(TfmSpecificPackageFileWithRecursiveDir->WithMetadataValue('Extension', '.aar'))" />
    </ItemGroup>
  </Target>

</Project>
